    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc8dd8ef_0fb03faf",
        "filename": "fs/hwsdcardfs/dentry.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133869
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-20T03:59:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that is OK to spin_unlock(\u0026cast-\u003ed_lock); here.\nBecause, if you take a look at the remaining code of \"dput\" after\nd_delete(dentry), it has only\n\tif (unlikely(dentry-\u003ed_flags \u0026 DCACHE_OP_DELETE)) {\n\t\tif (dentry-\u003ed_op-\u003ed_delete(dentry))\n\t\t\tgoto kill_it;\n\t}\n\n\tdentry_lru_add(dentry);\n\n\tdentry-\u003ed_lockref.count--;    \u003c-- we have d_count \u003e 0\n\tspin_unlock(\u0026dentry-\u003ed_lock);\n\treturn;\n\nor dentry_kill\n\tstruct inode *inode \u003d dentry-\u003ed_inode;\n\tstruct dentry *parent \u003d NULL;\n\n\tif (inode \u0026\u0026 unlikely(!spin_trylock(\u0026inode-\u003ei_lock)))\n\t\tgoto failed;\n        ...\nfailed:\n\tspin_unlock(\u0026dentry-\u003ed_lock);  \u003c-- take a look here\n\treturn dentry; /* try again with same dentry */\n\nboth are spin_unlock(\u0026dentry-\u003ed_lock); safe.",
      "parentUuid": "7328ebae_d4e7d2d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "9d6251bd6b7e4e69d43f9ace4fd3a3b6e1dcbeec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98138d71_8d96c0ba",
        "filename": "fs/hwsdcardfs/dentry.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133869
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-20T05:09:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "and before d_delete, you can see its only\nfast_dput\n    \t/*\n\t * If we have a d_op-\u003ed_delete() operation, we sould not\n\t * let the dentry count go to zero, so use \"put_or_lock\".\n\t */\n\tif (unlikely(dentry-\u003ed_flags \u0026 DCACHE_OP_DELETE))\n\t\treturn lockref_put_or_lock(\u0026dentry-\u003ed_lockref);\n        ...\n\ndput\n        fast_dput\n\n\t/* Slow case: now with the dentry lock held */\n\trcu_read_unlock();\n\n\tWARN_ON(d_in_lookup(dentry));\n\n\t/* Unreachable? Get rid of it */\n\tif (unlikely(d_unhashed(dentry)))\n\t\tgoto kill_it;\n\n\tif (unlikely(dentry-\u003ed_flags \u0026 DCACHE_DISCONNECTED))\n\t\tgoto kill_it;\n\n\tif (unlikely(dentry-\u003ed_flags \u0026 DCACHE_OP_DELETE)) {\n\t\tif (dentry-\u003ed_op-\u003ed_delete(dentry)) \u003c-- we are here\n\t\t\tgoto kill_it;\n\t}\n so you can think\n    1) d_count \u003e 0\n    2) after lockref_put_or_lock and before dentry-\u003ed_op-\u003ed_delete(dentry), only a few check, if we unlock and relock d_lock again, we redo \n            if (unlikely(d_unhashed(dentry)))\n\t\tgoto kill_it;\n       to confirm whether we should kill or into LRU.\n   that is equal to delay lock d_lock with d_count \u003e 0.\n\nthere here will be no race.",
      "parentUuid": "7328ebae_d4e7d2d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "9d6251bd6b7e4e69d43f9ace4fd3a3b6e1dcbeec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
